ADJTIME(2)	    UNIX Programmer's Manual	       ADJTIME(2)





NOTES  (FGX)
     The correction is applied at 66 microseconds a clock tick,
     0.4 percent, and at ten times that while more than a second
     remains.  The delta is rounded to a whole number of those
     steps, as FreeBSD rounds it, so that the correction ends
     exactly.  Olddelta returns the part of the previous correc-
     tion not yet applied.














































